{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2020",
    "useDefineForClassFields": true,
    "lib": ["ES2020", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "module": "ESNext",
    "skipLibCheck": true,

    /* Bundler mode */
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "jsx": "react-jsx",

    /* Linting */
    "strict": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "noUnusedParameters": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    /* noUncheckedIndexedAccess: attempted 2026-07-27 and deferred, per
       ADR-A10, which set the threshold at 30 errors. Measured: 59 -- 16 in
       src, 43 in tests. Not silenced with `any`: there are zero `any` in
       src and that is worth more than this flag.

       Where they are, so the next attempt starts with a map rather than a
       measurement. src: ImageGrid 5, CompareModal 4, seedPrompts 2,
       UpgradeModal 2, ModelColumn 2, useAuthStore 1. tests:
       useToastStore.test 16, then GenerationPanel.test and client.test at 4
       each. The source tree alone is within the threshold, so enabling it
       for src ahead of tests is a viable route if someone wants one.

       exactOptionalPropertyTypes is deliberately not attempted at all --
       ADR-A10. */
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": false,

    /* Path aliases */
    "baseUrl": ".",
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["src/*"]
    }
  },
  "include": ["src", "tests"]
}
